341	QUY TRÌNH ĐÀO TẠO, ĐIỀU KIỆN TỐT NGHIỆP	<p>Theo quy chế hiện hành của Bộ Giáo dục và Đào tạo và các quy định của Học viện Kỹ thuật mật mã.</p>
90	Overview	<p>The Information Technology (IT) training program of the Cryptography Technical Academy is designed to train university-level human resources (Engineers) in the field of Information Technology in the context of international integration and digital transformation. Graduates are equipped with future professional skills in Information Technology including expertise, political qualities, professional ethics, and soft skills. The training content combines theory and practice, aiming to help students effectively apply knowledge of Artificial Intelligence to solve practical problems. At the same time, the Information Technology training program is part of the Academy's development strategy with the educational philosophy of "Knowledge - Creativity - Ethics - Responsibility" aiming to train human resources "both talented and virtuous" to contribute to the common development of the country and humanity.</p><p><strong>Program name:</strong> Full-time undergraduate program in Information Technology</p><p><strong>Education level:</strong> University</p><p><strong>Degree:</strong> Bachelor and Engineer</p><p><strong>Training major:</strong> Information Technology</p><p><strong>Major code:</strong> 7480101</p><p><strong>Major:</strong> Embedded software engineering and mobile software</p><p><strong>Training type:</strong> Full-time</p><p><strong>Program code: </strong>KMC.1.1.1 The program is built according to the CDIO output standard approach (Conceive – Design – Implement – Operate)</p><p><strong>Total course knowledge volume:</strong> 176 credits.</p><p><strong>Total training time: 4 or 5 years.</strong></p>
